></tr><tr><td>ja</td><td>ya</td><td>ja</td><td>ya</td><td></td><td>ja</td><td>ya</td><td>ja</td><td>ya</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>he-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td></td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>&amp;nbsp;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table></td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.152.10","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"Below, (Vande Bhāratam) is being written in saṅkhyā lipi (number notation). Explaining the number notation once more: the number written above or below a syllable is counted onward by taking the number given on the syllable before it as zero, and whatever note results from the written number is the note to be played. If the number is below the syllable, move that many downward; if the number is written above the syllable, move that many upward. Every number is tied to its neighbouring note on the left. This song will be begun from 'Sa'."},{"id":"BV.152.11","kind":"heading","n":null,"level":2,"text":"Rāga Des, tāla Kaharvā"},{"id":"BV.152.12","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><tr><td><table class=\"bv-layout\"><tr><td></td><td></td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>vaṃ</td><td>-</td><td>de</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table></td><td>|<table class=\"bv-layout\"><tr><td></td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td>mā</td><td>-</td><td>ta</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>2</td></tr></table></td><td>|<table class=\"bv-layout\"><tr><td>2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>ram</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>&amp;nbsp;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table></td><td>|<table class=\"bv-layout\"><tr><td></td><td></td><td>2</td><td>&amp;nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>vaṃ</t